  "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{log}_{3}⁡(-9x)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{3}⁡(-9x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246608/assets/41378635430091e24674e22dbc45105bedd7af55410ba6069057f7a37b2025fc.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{log}_{3}⁡(-9x)=\\infty \n$$",
